 palette expansion, but should retain the same metric profile, stable-selection,
 terrain-sampling and bounded-instancing contract.
 
+### Terrain-contact and public-realm microdetail integration
+
+The interactive public realm now uses one constructible vertical datum rather
+than unrelated offsets for prepared ground, carriageway, markings, curbs,
+sidewalks and tactile surfaces. Street stations probe the left edge, centre and
+right edge within the existing ray budget, reject isolated roofs, canopies and
+coarse-tile misses, and interpolate the resulting cross-slope through ribbons,
+curbs, furniture and planting. Parks apply the same robust local contact rule
+to primary program objects, family microdetail and fixed assemblies. Prepared
+site surfaces overlap the independently rasterized Google Tiles mask by a
+bounded tolerance so the replacement edge cannot reveal a white pixel seam.
+
+The five executable park families now carry bounded, deterministic signature
+details such as native planting clumps, stone, lighting, bins, cycle parking,
+bollards, picnic tables and tree grates. Their complete rendered footprints
+must remain inside the park, clear fitted paths, water, fixed program and
+maintenance zones, and remain collision-free after scale variation. Water
+ecology families reserve inlet, outlet, wet-shelf and maintenance functions and
+do not receive recreational furniture by generic fallback.
+
+Executable street families now distribute drains, sidewalk joints, bins,
+cycle racks, protection bollards and planting cells across the complete usable
+segment instead of filling its first end. Woonerf chicanes, green-alley
+bioswales, accessible four-way crossings and roundabout approach markings are
+separate family-aware assemblies. Signal equipment is a hierarchy decision,
+not an automatic decoration on every four-way local intersection. All
+placement loops and instance counts are finite before district-scale rollout.
+
